# PETER PAN — Locked Decisions (DO NOT re-litigate)

These decisions are final. Never change, "improve," or reopen them. If a task
appears to conflict with any of these, STOP and ask — do not pick silently.

## Contracts
- Guardrail response schema is exactly `{passed: bool, flags: list[str], reason: str}`.
  Never `{valid, reason}`, never `{pass, ...}`. Pydantic model `GuardrailResult`
  in `contracts.py` with `extra="forbid"` is the single source of truth.
- Predictor has exactly **6 incident classes**. The field name is `incident_class`.
  The 3-way routing category is DERIVED from the 6 classes at the n8n Router
  (node 8) — it is not a second predictor field and not a class-count change.
- Severity levels are P1–P4 only. There is no P5.

## Scope (rejected — do not reintroduce)
- No Twilio / voice integration.
- No Slack Block Kit HITL flow.
- No live outage-bridge / call integration.
- Feedback loop (reviewer queue → retrain) is ROADMAP ONLY — slides, not code.

## Infrastructure
- IaC: CloudFormation (not Terraform) — locked due to the two-week constraint.
- Single-node EC2 t3.large with docker-compose. No Kubernetes, no multi-node.
- Demo-scale synthetic data only. Never real production data, never real
  customer identifiers.

## LLM tier
- Fixture-first: every demo scenario must work from deterministic fixtures
  with zero external API calls. Live LLM paths (Bedrock/Gemini/Ollama) are
  additive fallbacks, never dependencies of the demo path.

## Secrets & safety
- Secrets never in committable files. `.env` from the template only; verify
  `.gitignore` coverage before adding any new config file.
- Deterministic safety floors override LLM-stated values (the "LLM extracts;
  the service decides" principle).

## Workflow
- Audit before action. Phased gates before destructive operations
  (delete/rename/history rewrite): show the plan, wait for approval.
- Never merge locally to main — always push branch → PR → merge on green CI.
